# Learner Profile: George

## Who
- Name: George
- Birthday: 2021-06-23 (age ~5)
- First language: Chinese (Traditional); English is a second language

## Interests
- TV / video: Paw Patrol, Doctor Binocs
- Books: bedtime stories, Oxford Reading Tree, recently Dragon Masters (read aloud to him)
- Theme preference for lessons: dragons and adventure (primary); rescue squad / fun science as secondary

## Current reading level
- Listening comprehension is stronger than independent reading
- Parents usually read aloud; he is beginning to try reading himself
- Target difficulty: Oxford Reading Tree Stage 2–3 (short complete sentences, high-frequency words)
- Needs heavy pronunciation support (tap-to-speak, slow TTS)

## Teaching goals
- Move from listen-only to guided independent reading
- Every lesson must include: vocabulary preview, story, comprehension with instant feedback, sight-word practice, and a teacher/parent follow-up notes area
- Keep language warm, encouraging, and age-appropriate (no scary or violent content)

## Project workflow
- Lessons live under `lessons/` as self-contained HTML
- Images under `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/`
- Publish via GitHub Pages (repo root); fixed URL for the tutor
- When user says「發佈」or「publish」: commit lesson changes and push to `main` so Pages updates
